{
 "schema": "tick-store-targets-1",
 "what": "Every target of BENCHMARKS.md, each stated host a row: the target, where its figure is read in a committed results file, and how it is judged. scripts/render_results.py reads only this file and the results files, computes each verdict from the value and the target, and writes the README's Targets block. A row with no figure says why; nothing here is a figure.",
 "expressions": "A value is {\"path\": [...]}, keys into the part's file, where \"@headline\" is the headline_variant of the object above; {\"case\": name, \"field\": [...]}, a bench results case; {\"cases_median\": pattern, \"field\": [...]}, the median of a field over every case the pattern matches; {\"best\": column, \"family\": f, \"not_family\": f}, the fewest bits a value of any codec of a codec-eval column; {\"codec\": name, \"column\": column, \"field\": f}; {\"store_bits\": [columns], \"per\": column}, a store-size file's bits a value over those columns; {\"min_variant\": [system, path...]}, the smallest over a comparison system's variants; {\"div\" | \"mul\": [a, b]} with numbers as constants.",
